WEBVTT

NOTE Draft cue timing follows measured scene audio and word count. Review spoken word alignment before publication.

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.867
Welcome to Resgrid Academy. In this lesson, we will record routine checks and

00:00:04.867 --> 00:00:09.734
missed work. Paper checks make it difficult to see which apparatus was inspected

00:00:09.734 --> 00:00:14.601
and which scheduled checks were missed. We will explain the features, the setup

00:00:14.601 --> 00:00:17.970
decisions, and a practical way to check the result.

00:00:18.570 --> 00:00:23.545
A daily apparatus check is scheduled for each engine, and the weekly compliance

00:00:23.545 --> 00:00:28.521
report shows any missed checks. Recorded checks show what was inspected and what

00:00:28.521 --> 00:00:33.496
was missed. The examples in this series use a fictional department and are

00:00:33.496 --> 00:00:35.410
teaching scenarios, not default settings.

00:00:36.010 --> 00:00:41.723
Checklist Templates. Ready-made checklists for common checks. Start from a template or build

00:00:41.723 --> 00:00:43.920
a checklist for each apparatus.

00:00:44.520 --> 00:00:51.040
Checklists. Checklists members complete. Create the checklists members complete on paper today.

00:00:51.640 --> 00:00:57.486
Checklist schedules and due work. Recurring schedules and due checks. Schedule each checklist

00:00:57.486 --> 00:01:03.331
and choose who completes it. Availability also depends on Checklists. Check access in

00:01:03.331 --> 00:01:04.680
the target department.

00:01:05.280 --> 00:01:10.098
New Checklist. Create a checklist. Pick the checks you do on paper today

00:01:10.098 --> 00:01:11.580
and who completes them.

00:01:12.180 --> 00:01:17.983
Checklist compliance reports. Completed, skipped and overdue checks over time. Pick the checks

00:01:17.983 --> 00:01:23.785
you do on paper today and who completes them. Availability also depends on

00:01:23.785 --> 00:01:26.910
Checklists. Check access in the target department.

00:01:27.510 --> 00:01:33.026
For the training scenario, work in this order. Step 1. Start from a

00:01:33.026 --> 00:01:38.541
checklist template or build the approved checks. Step 2. Assign the checklist and

00:01:38.541 --> 00:01:44.057
set its recurring schedule. Step 3. Complete a demo check, record a defect,

00:01:44.057 --> 00:01:45.330
and review compliance.

00:01:45.930 --> 00:01:51.847
Now verify the result. Compare due checks with completed, skipped, and overdue results.

00:01:51.847 --> 00:01:57.763
Confirm defects have an assigned follow-up owner. A common problem to watch for:

00:01:57.763 --> 00:02:03.680
A completion report documents recorded checks. A failed item still requires action through

00:02:03.680 --> 00:02:05.500
the department repair process.

00:02:06.100 --> 00:02:11.032
Your practice task is simple. Complete a daily Engine 1 check and leave

00:02:11.032 --> 00:02:15.964
a second demo check overdue. Confirm that the compliance view distinguishes both. Record

00:02:15.964 --> 00:02:20.896
the result, who owns the follow-up, and when it should be reviewed. Use

00:02:20.896 --> 00:02:24.690
the linked feature scripts for the detailed screen recording plan.

